# Repo Governance

- Treat this repository as planning and documentation first.
- Do not implement application runtime code in this repo except inside intended submodules.
- Before editing in `vagabond/app/` or `valesor/www.*` submodules, explicitly confirm the target repo boundary and task intent.
- Prefer updating tracker artifacts (`personal/project-tracker/`) when work changes project status, priorities, or automation state.

## Safety Checks

- If a request might modify app code outside submodules, stop and redirect to the correct app repository path.
- Preserve unrelated in-progress changes; never revert user work unless explicitly requested.
- Keep edits scoped to the smallest set of files that satisfy the request.

## Commit Guidance

- Use concise, intent-first commit messages (Conventional Commits preferred).
- For tracker updates, use scopes like `tracker`, `docs`, `rules`, or `skills`.
- Mention the reason for the change, not only the files touched.
